Mirror pages: a small rule in scripts/build.py typeset(). typeset() also needs the page kind and the render language (render_page passes meta['kind'] and lang), and runs smarten(soup, path, lang) only when kind == 'mirror'. The same rule covers issues single-quotes-nested, double-quotes-curly, ellipsis-character and dot-leaders:
LEADER_PAGES = {'article/Where+to+Find.html', 'article/Icons+of+the+Mother+of+God.html'}
LEADER = re.compile(r'(?<=[A-Za-z)!])\s*\.{2,}\s*(?=[A-Z0-9])')
SMART = [
  (re.compile(r'(?<=[!?])\.{4} ?(?=[A-Z])'), '… '),
  (re.compile(r'\.{4}(?=[A-Z])'), '…. '),
  (re.compile(r'\.\.\.'), '…'),
  (re.compile(r'(?<=[A-Za-z])\x27(?=[A-Za-z])'), '’'),
  (re.compile(r'(?<=[A-Za-z0-9.,;:!?)\]…])\x27(?![A-Za-z0-9])'), '’'),
  (re.compile(r'(?:^|(?<=[\s(\[“]))\x27(?=[A-Za-z0-9…])'), '‘'),
  (re.compile(r'(?:^|(?<=[\s(\[‘]))\x22(?=\S)'), '“'),
  (re.compile(r'(?<=\S)\x22(?=[\s.,;:!?)\]]|$)'), '”'),
]
def smarten(soup, path, lang):
  for s in list(soup.find_all(string=True)):
    if isinstance(s, Comment) or effective_lang(s, lang) != 'en' or URL_TEXT.fullmatch(s.strip()): continue
    t = LEADER.sub(' – ', str(s)) if path in LEADER_PAGES else str(s)
    for rx, rep in SMART: t = rx.sub(rep, t)
    if re.search(r'[\x27\x22]|\.\.\.', t): sys.exit(f'build: {path}: a straight quote or three dots the rule cannot place: {t.strip()[:60]!r}')
    if t != s: s.replace_with(NavigableString(t))
The effective_lang check skips Russian text (creed.html, pravmir.html) and any lang='de'. On the ru/ copy of a mirror page the English blocks carry lang='en', so they are fixed there too. Frozen pages, by hand in both language files: about_orthodoxy.html:42 and ru/about_orthodoxy.html:42 'The Church's Prayer for the Dead' → 'The Church’s Prayer for the Dead'. Local page: privacy.html:9 'website's' → 'website’s' (ru/privacy.html has nothing to change).
